Original bug 31: a resting pad aim stick swings the aim onto the player, and a drifting one twitches it, since pad aim
has no deadzone. The fix keeps the aim's last direction, 60 units out, inside stick radius 0.2, as the Python port's
local input and the client's recorded runs do (host/session.inc live_input). Recorded runs aim from their recording
(seams/pad-aim.patch), so this reaches only the runs the original plays.
--- a/decomp/1.9/crimsonland/gameplay/player_update_heading.cpp
+++ b/decomp/1.9/crimsonland/gameplay/player_update_heading.cpp
@@ -1049,6 +1049,13 @@
             D3DXVec2Normalize(&pad, &pad);
             float distance = aim_length * cv_padAimDistMul->value + 42.0f;
             *(vec2_t *)&player->aim = pad * distance + *(vec2_t *)&player->position;
+            if (!portable_preserve_bugs && length <= 0.2f) {
+                float radians = player->aim_heading - 1.5707964f;
+                vec2_t rest;
+                rest.x = cosf(radians) * 60.0f;
+                rest.y = sinf(radians) * 60.0f;
+                *(vec2_t *)&player->aim = rest + *(vec2_t *)&player->position;
+            }
             }
             player->aim_heading =
                 VEC2_Angle(
